{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "07XK", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-limits}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:49e9cafdfdcadd4005c82272376faed3deef5460b321bf0cb9060518db88467c", "source_text": "Limit preserving", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d4aefc9646a5079f47828f7d250dcf6b79e725113548bd7e9cb4995e3a9b05df", "unit_id": "tag:07XK:title"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "07XK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p : \\mathcal{X} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{criteria-section-limit-preserving}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{examples-section-limit-preserving}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:46c2f089503b14f7cf370813995ebfbf1474c57923cc1b646b2706ac66ef9f50", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:516def3c72de75c82d5eb5b86c7886fba07592be88defa710d0f8df5ace16ae9", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe morphism <MATH_0001> is limit preserving\non objects, as defined in Criteria for Representability, Section\n<REF_0001>, if the functor of the definition\nbelow is essentially surjective. However, the example\nin Examples, Section <REF_0002>\nshows that this isn't equivalent to being limit preserving.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:67d3af05bab0882bea64bd75a8e353d20fc0162f350371f4ec3cd3a56ba090ee", "unit_id": "tag:07XK:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "07XK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$T$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$T = \\lim T_i$", "MATH_0008": "$T_i$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\colim \\mathcal{X}_{T_i} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{X}_T\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-limit-preserving}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c14a39401667105e659a1669a0b2ae6bfc60357ddd8d1160db7f20801ec5235a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a6bac9a3fc31d56548d01f3e476ec5fa04f1efe3867078eb47f08a7f1b5d534b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a category fibred in groupoids\nover <MATH_0003>. We say <MATH_0004> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>limit preserving<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif for every affine scheme <MATH_0005> over <MATH_0006> which is a limit <MATH_0007>\nof a directed inverse system of affine schemes <MATH_0008> over <MATH_0009>, we have\nan equivalence\n<MATH_0010>\nof fibre categories.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2edbc35d5fa62c4be5aa15f578a16c7fa020c279c0a85763aead89bc28739d55", "unit_id": "tag:07XL:statement"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "07XK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$x, y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$T_i$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\mathcal{X}_T}(x|_T, y|_T) =\n\\colim_{i' \\geq i} \\Mor_{\\mathcal{X}_{T_{i'}}}(x|_{T_{i'}}, y|_{T_{i'}})\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X}_T$", "MATH_0006": "$T_i$", "MATH_0007": "$i$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathit{Isom}_\\mathcal{X}(x, y)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-definition-mor-presheaf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f15a6894d6f01aa0852715bd351ff5998618529c6c761e301673cc85e17276b6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:60dc70db3a669d124769671b0180e32df67a1fcc76fce97c637dfd6596dcf7ef", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe spell out what this means. First, given objects <MATH_0001> of <MATH_0002>\nover <MATH_0003> we should have\n<MATH_0004>\nand second every object of <MATH_0005> is isomorphic to the restriction\nof an object over <MATH_0006> for some <MATH_0007>. Note that the first condition means\nthat the presheaves <MATH_0008> (see\nStacks, Definition <REF_0001>)\nare limit preserving.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:963fbfd78b969ba2e4ebd48a133d9daf52a1e28c9601b86d0b9bbca5cd39eb7e", "unit_id": "tag:07XK:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "07XK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$p : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$q : \\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$1$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{Z} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{Z}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fibre-product-limit-preserving}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a95ec7860387de01a00f0c7a8790f6df95e1b9be0f29a5ba430db6487e0311cc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e5ebbb0b8a57255f1a29185b6abd0ebf994e90ea93ccf5803b1f3afb9bf85874", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> and\n<MATH_0003> be <MATH_0004>-morphisms of categories\nfibred in groupoids over <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0006> and\n<MATH_0007> are limit preserving on objects and\n<MATH_0008> is limit preserving, then\n<MATH_0009> is\nlimit preserving on objects.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0010>, <MATH_0011>,\nand <MATH_0012> are limit preserving, then so\nis <MATH_0013>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:53c9c0c60f896366f5999a6503bd17f0311582ce9df73aa0d20e13a08bf615e9", "unit_id": "tag:07XM:statement"}
